{
  "id": "endogenous-cue",
  "term": "endogenous cue",
  "definition": "An endogenous cue is a signal that guides attention through a person’s goals, expectations, or learned knowledge rather than through the cue’s immediate physical salience. In this source, emotional information can function as an endogenous cue when people know it predicts where a target is likely to appear and use that association to direct attention.",
